(7810733, 1304091, 30982, '<td valign="top">
Well seen and captured, this photograph has a bit of a gloomy feel to it.  In one sense, it could be interpreted as commentary on the state of the country in the US at the moment.  But it can also be seen as a moment of clarity and clearing after the storm.  And to me, if your photograph can evoke differing emotional reactions from your viewers, you’ve done a pretty good job.</td>', 'Well seen and captured, this photograph has a bit of a gloomy feel to it.  In one sense, it could be interpreted as commentary on the state of the country in the US at the moment.  But it can also be seen as a moment of clarity and clearing after the storm.  And to me, if your photograph can evoke differing emotional reactions from your viewers, you’ve done a pretty good job.', '2026-02-24 21:26:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(7810734, 1304287, 30982, '<td valign="top">
Grainy, black and white photographs have always appealed to me, perhaps because they create a mood rather than simply providing a record.  Here it imparts a bit of a rainy afternoon sadness.  The water spots and vignetting nicely balance the lines of the structure, too.</td>', 'Grainy, black and white photographs have always appealed to me, perhaps because they create a mood rather than simply providing a record.  Here it imparts a bit of a rainy afternoon sadness.  The water spots and vignetting nicely balance the lines of the structure, too.', '2026-02-24 21:26:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(7810735, 1304281, 30982, '<td valign="top">
First of all – pigeon!  I adore photographs of pigeons.  It’s a thing – can’t really explain it.  Not just any pigeon, though - this one is most definitely on a mission and can’t be bothered to stay in the frame.   To me, it’s a lovely, light-hearted snippet of life.  I really like how the processing lends itself to the “je ne sais quoi” feel of this, too.   ‘Tis a great example of how an “out-of-balance” photograph can be perfectly balanced after all.</td>', 'First of all – pigeon!  I adore photographs of pigeons.  It’s a thing – can’t really explain it.  Not just any pigeon, though - this one is most definitely on a mission and can’t be bothered to stay in the frame.   To me, it’s a lovely, light-hearted snippet of life.  I really like how the processing lends itself to the “je ne sais quoi” feel of this, too.   ‘Tis a great example of how an “out-of-balance” photograph can be perfectly balanced after all.', '2026-02-24 21:27:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7810736, 1304212, 30982, '<td valign="top">
There is a quiet determination and grace in this photograph.  The exposure and toning contribute to the overall feel, but my favorite part is you can “see” him walking because of those footsteps in the snow, his stride short but sure.  This capture of a simple everyday moment in time is one of the reasons I love photography.</td>', 'There is a quiet determination and grace in this photograph.  The exposure and toning contribute to the overall feel, but my favorite part is you can “see” him walking because of those footsteps in the snow, his stride short but sure.  This capture of a simple everyday moment in time is one of the reasons I love photography.', '2026-02-24 21:28:25.000000', NULL, 0),
